{
  "title": "城市記得她",
  "title_en": "The City Remembers Her",
  "series": "神話未完成",
  "series_en": "Myths in the Making",
  "volume": 11,
  "model": "史旺姬",
  "creator": "史旺基 Swanky",
  "slug": "swanky-ji-city-remembers-her",
  "date": "2026-10-23",
  "count": 36,
  "cover_photo": 9,
  "setting": "珍珠母鋪成的城",
  "subtitle": "昨日的路，容得下今日的方向。",
  "subtitle_en": "Yesterday’s paths leave room for today’s directions.",
  "lead": "女王停步，城市把久遠的腳步交還給她。珍珠母的表面浮出磨痕，赤足、鞋底與車輪曾經走過的方向再次可見。她沿路遇見果籃、桌子、柱子，也遇見仍在使用這座城的人。記憶保存了一條路，生活卻可以從旁邊經過。這本書讓兩種時間留在同一個地面上：貝內的舊痕，以及今日腳步帶來的粉塵。",
  "lead_en": "When the queen pauses, the city returns its older footsteps to her. Worn traces emerge in mother-of-pearl: directions once taken by bare feet, shoes and wheels become visible again. Along the way she encounters baskets, tables and columns, and the people who still use this city. Memory preserves a path; life can pass beside it. Two times share the same ground in this book: old traces within the shell and dust carried by today’s footsteps.",
  "statement": "女王停步，城市把久遠的腳步交還給她。珍珠母的表面浮出磨痕，赤足、鞋底與車輪曾經走過的方向再次可見。她沿路遇見果籃、桌子、柱子，也遇見仍在使用這座城的人。記憶保存了一條路，生活卻可以從旁邊經過。這本書讓兩種時間留在同一個地面上：貝內的舊痕，以及今日腳步帶來的粉塵。\n\n一條舊路抵住了柱腳。另一條曾經折返，也曾有人在中途停下。女王能喚回這些方向，卻不替居民決定今天怎麼走。新的粉痕會鬆散、變淡；有些步伐只屬於走過的當下。她放下外套、解開髮簪，讓城裡的人替她重綁辮子，再把髮簪留在果籃裡。最後，她坐在交易廣場安靜的一角，外套放在身旁，雙手攤開；地上的新粉痕都往外走。城市記得她，也繼續容納此刻。",
  "statement_en": "When the queen pauses, the city returns its older footsteps to her. Worn traces emerge in mother-of-pearl: directions once taken by bare feet, shoes and wheels become visible again. Along the way she encounters baskets, tables and columns, and the people who still use this city. Memory preserves a path; life can pass beside it. Two times share the same ground in this book: old traces within the shell and dust carried by today’s footsteps.\n\nAn old route reaches the foot of a column. Another once turned back; someone paused along it. The queen can recall these directions, but she does not choose how residents must walk today. Fresh powder loosens and fades. Some footsteps belong only to the moment in which they are taken. She sets her jacket down, takes the pin from her hair, lets someone in the city retie her braid, and leaves the pin in a fruit basket. In the end she sits at a quiet corner of the trading square, the jacket beside her, her hands open; the fresh powder prints on the ground all lead away from her. The city remembers her, and continues to make room for the present.",
  "afterword": "一條舊路抵住了柱腳。另一條曾經折返，也曾有人在中途停下。女王能喚回這些方向，卻不替居民決定今天怎麼走。新的粉痕會鬆散、變淡；有些步伐只屬於走過的當下。她放下外套、解開髮簪，讓城裡的人替她重綁辮子，再把髮簪留在果籃裡。最後，她坐在交易廣場安靜的一角，外套放在身旁，雙手攤開；地上的新粉痕都往外走。城市記得她，也繼續容納此刻。",
  "afterword_en": "An old route reaches the foot of a column. Another once turned back; someone paused along it. The queen can recall these directions, but she does not choose how residents must walk today. Fresh powder loosens and fades. Some footsteps belong only to the moment in which they are taken. She sets her jacket down, takes the pin from her hair, lets someone in the city retie her braid, and leaves the pin in a fruit basket. In the end she sits at a quiet corner of the trading square, the jacket beside her, her hands open; the fresh powder prints on the ground all lead away from her. The city remembers her, and continues to make room for the present.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "創作從Meenakshi的女王形象與Madurai的城市敘事展開。Paranjothi的《Tiruvilaiyadal Puranam》中，技藝、武藝、加冕與統治相連；城市則與神的在場彼此構成。本冊把這份主動性轉成一種觀看時間的能力，讓街道與居民各自保有方向。",
  "story_en": "The work begins with Meenakshi’s image as queen and the urban narratives of Madurai. In Paranjothi’s Tiruvilaiyadal Puranam, learning, martial skill, coronation and rule form a sequence; the city and divine presence shape one another. Here that agency becomes a way of seeing time, while streets and residents retain directions of their own.",
  "sources_zh": "故事參考：Madurai District — Sri Meenakshi–Sundareswarar Temple（https://madurai.nic.in/tourist-place/sri-meenakshi-sundareswarar-temple/）；Project Madurai — Tiruvilaiyadal Puranam, part 1, 552–560（https://www.projectmadurai.org/pm_etexts/utf8/pmuni0463_01.html）",
  "sources_en": "Story references: Madurai District — Sri Meenakshi–Sundareswarar Temple (https://madurai.nic.in/tourist-place/sri-meenakshi-sundareswarar-temple/); Project Madurai — Tiruvilaiyadal Puranam, part 1, 552–560 (https://www.projectmadurai.org/pm_etexts/utf8/pmuni0463_01.html)",
  "credit": "創作與攝影概念：史旺基 · 角色：史旺姬",
  "credit_en": "Creative direction and photographic concept: Swanky · Character: Swanky Ji",
